<!--Post: 9185--><!--Time: 1109412664-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9185"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 2:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is all academic now – but, I would like to clean out my BTK closet. I invite all fellow hunters to do the same on this thread. <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ <BR> <BR>In the early 1950s he built and operated a ham radio. <BR>-WPD Nov 30, 04 <BR> <BR>Ham Radio = Police Radio <BR> <BR>A phone call save them &#40;the Vian children&#41; <BR>-BTK Feb. 10/78 <BR> <BR>This never made sense to me. How a bout a dispatch call that was too close for comfort coming over the scanner he kept in his murder kit. That’s what save&#40;d&#41; them. <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ <BR> <BR>Grandfather played the fiddle and died of a lung disease = Old Manor violent asphyxiation. <BR>What happened on Oldmanor Road? Anyone? <BR> <BR>- - - - - - - - - - - - - <BR>  <BR>In Cold Blood <BR> <BR>The bloody boot print at The Otero’s was intentionally made by BTK in tribute to Perry Smith and Dick Hickock as well as the blind cords, the blaring radio, the use of the basement and the overturned purse. BTK disguised himself as the dark complected Perry Smith. <BR> <BR>The fingerprint on the chair was, as Ed Neil suggested, a Zodiac tribute. If there is no match then I believe BTK brought a “spare” finger on ice from an earlier victim.  <BR> <BR>Young ladies’ brassieres in the 1970s were never dark in color. It was a bathing suit top. It was her secret. <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ <BR> <BR>Secret Witness <BR> <BR>The Otero Case letter was left in a mechanical engineering textbook in the central branch of the Wichita Public Library in October of 1974. I don’t believe the actual date of discovery has been made public.   <BR> <BR>October 15th 1974 was a Tuesday. The only other Tuesday the 15th in 1974 was in January, the date of the Otero murders. The temperature in Wichita that day ranged from 63c to 33c. The WPL central branch was open until a very nippy 9:00pm. <BR> <BR>I think the book is Basic Machines and How They Work, by the U.S Bureau of Naval Personnel. <BR> <BR>The gloves really were superfluous, outside of keeping those icy hands warm. The applied physics section in a public library occupies a lonely aisle. It’s not exactly the kind of place one would go to meet girls. <BR> <BR>If the coast was clear, two handkerchiefs would get the job done nicely. <BR> <BR>This drop was meticulously planned and, as always, he created a disguise to suit his needs. <BR> <BR>BTK may have waited several days to announce the existence of the letter. As Ed Neil stated, October 22, 1974 was “precisely five years to the day after someone claiming to be the Zodiac called Oakland PD… <BR> <BR> I believe the WPD placed a duplicate textbook back on the shelf after the discovery as they felt it could be the killer’s preferred point of distribution for future communication. <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ <BR> <BR>Something Nancy Fox said to BTK actually disturbs him to this day, no matter how much he punished her for it. It is part of the reason he telephoned if not entirely in tribute to Zodiac. <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ <BR> <BR>Kathryn Bright is a definite BTK victim. <BR> <BR>In addition to the fact that the perennially discreet WPD lists her as such, consider the parting shot from the Otero Case letter sent six months after the Bright attack. <BR> <BR>“P.S. Since sex criminals do not change their <BR>M.O. or by nature cannot do so, I will not <BR>change mine” <BR> <BR>BTK,  October 1974 <BR> <BR>After confirming his responsibility for the frenzy at the Oteros, a sex criminal attempts to erase any connection to the Bright fiasco. He was frightened of the eyewitness. <BR> <BR>A sex criminal had quite a struggle outside the death spot. <BR>A sex criminal changed his M.O. when he panicked. <BR>A sex criminal shied away from adult male victims for good after Kevin. <BR> <BR>_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
